    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "low",
      "note": "The file's hour names are Swahili numerals, not Sukuma; Sukuma speakers in Tanzania tell clock time with the Swahili loan system (saa tatu = 9:00), so I rotated the hours to East African reckoning and used the Swahili 'saa {h} na dakika ... / na nusu / kasoro robo' patterns. Result is correct for how time is actually said in Sukuma-land but it is Swahili, not Sukuma vocabulary. Noon 'adhuhuri' / midnight 'usiku gati' left as-is. Native Sukuma review needed."
    }
